From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:21:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: an optional notice of the playback mode, once
 per video
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode (off by default): a moment after a video starts, one
line says in which mode it plays: "Dolby Vision · FEL · 3840x2160 @ 23.976 Hz",
"Dolby Vision → HDR10" where a Dolby Vision video is sent as HDR10, "HDR10", and so
on. It is made from what the window system already publishes for the player
information (hades.src.hdrtype, hades.out.hdrtype, hades.dv.layers) and the mode of
the display, and waits until the same text has held for 1.5 s so that it does not
tell the mode of the first frames. It is told once per video, and not at all if the
output stays unknown for 8 s. The log has the same line.

CPlaybackModeAnnouncer is a header of its own, tested on the host in both directions.
